A single number, $\Delta = \gamma\beta - \alpha\delta$, decides whether a counting sequence curves up, runs straight, or curves down. Below you can explore the idea from every angle.

## 1. Play with the discriminant

Every classical total - powers of two, factorials, central binomials, Catalan numbers - is built by multiplying by a ratio $(\gamma n+\delta)/(\alpha n+\beta)$. Drag the four coefficients and watch $\Delta$ decide the log-behaviour instantly.

